        "original_id": "01407e07-dae5-5c0f-9c02-dac6bab03e95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Woodvale Historic District, Broad Top Township, Bedford County, Wells Township, Fulton County, Wood Township, Huntingdon County, Pennsylvania, Rockhill Furnace\n- Companies: Rockhill Iron and Coal Company, East Broad Top Railroad and Coal Company\n- Organizations: East Broad Top Railroad and Coal Company\n- Systems: narrow gauge historic railroad\n\nFacts:\n- Woodvale Historic District is a national historic district located in Broad Top Township, Bedford County, Wells Township, Fulton County, and Wood Township, Huntingdon County, Pennsylvania.\n- The buildings in Woodvale Historic District were built by the Rockhill Iron and Coal Company.\n- The East Broad Top Railroad and Coal Company is a for-profit narrow gauge historic railroad headquartered in Rockhill Furnace, Pennsylvania.\n- Rockhill Furnace is 19 miles north of Interstate 76 and 11 miles south of U.S. Route 22, the William Penn Highway.",
